From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ch13726a: 16-bit brightness, high byte first, on the AYN Thor

The DDIC CH13726A driver sends the brightness with
mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(), low byte first, over a 0-255 range.
The AYN Thor's bottom AMOLED reads it high byte first, so a level of n
arrived as n * 256: everything from about 16 up looked like full brightness
and only the lowest steps dimmed (measured on the Thor by stepping
255..1). On "ch13726a,thor" use the full 16-bit range, 0-65535, and
mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(). The panel looks the same from
about 4095 up, but the Thor's owner prefers it this way (tested against a
0-4095 range). The Retroid panels that share the driver keep the old
behaviour.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
@@ -203,7 +203,15 @@
 
 	dsi->mode_flags &= ~MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
-	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(dsi, brightness);
+	/*
+	 * The AYN Thor's bottom panel takes a 16-bit brightness, high byte
+	 * first. Sent low byte first, a level of n arrived as n * 256, so
+	 * everything from about 16 up was full brightness.
+	 */
+	if (bl->props.max_brightness > 255)
+		ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(dsi, brightness);
+	else
+		ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness(dsi, brightness);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -220,10 +228,11 @@
 ch13726a_create_backlight(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &dsi->dev;
+	int max = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "ch13726a,thor") ? 65535 : 255;
 	const struct backlight_properties props = {
 		.type = BACKLIGHT_RAW,
-		.brightness = 255,
-		.max_brightness = 255,
+		.brightness = max,
+		.max_brightness = max,
 	};
 
 	return devm_backlight_device_register(dev, dev_name(dev), dev, dsi,
